{"hash":"2b848bfbc924b75a","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":90.803,"said":"Har Har Mahadev! Come, walk with me. You are standing in the marble court of Baba Vishwanath, and before you rises his temple, its spire and dome shining with gold. But first, let me tell you where you are. This is Kashi, the city of light, which the world also calls Varanasi. The Shiva Purana says that before there were any worlds, the formless Shiva took form as Shiva and Shakti, and to give them a place for their tapas he made a city, five kroshas wide. That circle is still walked by pilgrims today, as the Panchakroshi. And when the world ends in the great dissolution and everything else is drowned, Shiva lifts this city on the point of his trident and holds it safe until creation begins again. That is why Kashi is called Avimukta, ‘never forsaken’: Shiva never leaves it. It is also called Anandavana, the forest of bliss. The temple trust says that the merit of darshan at every other Jyotirlinga comes to one who sees Vishwanath here. Yet many pilgrims do not rush in. First they go down to the Ganga, to bathe and fill their vessels. Let us do the same. Walk east with me, through the gate, toward the river.\n\nDid you know? The temple trust lists among Vishwanath’s pilgrims Adi Shankaracharya, Goswami Tulsidas, Guru Nanak, Ramakrishna Paramahamsa and Swami Vivekananda.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1125},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1141,"end":1288}],"words":[[0.098,0.252,0,3],[0.362,0.228,4,7],[0.603,0.661,8,15],[2.139,0.433,17,21],[2.74,0.312,23,27],[3.065,0.204,28,32],[3.281,0.288,33,35],[4.435,0.192,37,40],[4.639,0.132,41,44],[4.784,0.481,45,53],[5.276,0.096,54,56],[5.385,0.072,57,60],[5.469,0.397,61,67],[5.877,0.276,68,73],[6.166,0.12,74,76],[6.298,0.397,77,81],[6.707,0.685,82,92],[7.608,0.192,94,97],[7.812,0.361,98,104],[8.185,0.12,105,108],[8.317,0.505,109,114],[8.834,0.18,115,118],[9.026,0.505,119,125],[9.772,0.156,127,130],[9.94,0.493,131,136],[1